<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint-Palais, Pyrénées-Atlantiques</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint-Palais is a small town in the French Basque Country, in Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> conquered southern Navarre in 1512, the Albret kings of Navarre made it the seat of their government and courts for the lands north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, and it had a royal mint. Nearby, three of the pilgrim routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a> meet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-palais-pyrenees-atlantiques.jpg" alt="Saint-Palais, Pyrénées-Atlantiques" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angelsansailes · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eglise_de_Saint_palais.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
